# Commit Convention
> Standard: Conventional Commits

## Intent
Enforces Conventional Commits and intention-revealing commit boundaries.

## Rule
- Use Conventional Commit prefixes that reflect the type of change.
- Keep commits focused so each one tells a coherent story.
- Avoid bundling unrelated refactors with behavior changes.

## References

- [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/)

